{"t": 1793334807.2546592, "kind": "assistant", "content": "**Final design: P=9, Q=7, mode=RNE**\n\n* `synthesize_area`: acc=**11520**, block=26020, total=**37540**\n* Baseline P=24 exact-Q RNE: acc=21486, block=25856, total=47342\n* **Saving:** 9966 acc transistors = **46.4% accumulator saving**; 9802 total = **20.7% total saving**\n* `verify_rtl P9/Q7/RNE`: **0 mismatches / 1000 vectors** - PASS\n* `evaluate_accuracy confirm=true`:\n  * delta = **-0.126%**, 95% CI **[-0.558%, +0.317%]**\n  * upper end **0.32% <= +1.0%** - PASS\n\nScreening (4 seg, ~\u00b11.5% noise) + 2 confirms = 9/10 accuracy calls used.\n\n**What I learned:**\n1. **Q is the area knob, not P.** P 24\u219210 exact-Q only 21486\u219216490 acc. Adding Q=8: P10 exact 16490\u219212456, P12 exact 18176\u219213702. Block-product itself ~25.5-26k always - Q pre-rounding shrinks the *accumulator adder/shifter*, not the fixed product.\n2. **RNE mandatory, RZ catastrophic.** P9/Q7 RZ screening +53.76% vs RNE -0.51% for ~400T saving (11520\u219211106). RZ bias accumulates in long dot-product sums.\n3. **Sharp cliff at P8/P7:** P9/Q7 confirm -0.13% [-0.56,0.32] PASS; P8/Q7 confirm +0.76% [0.13,1.44] FAIL (upper>1%); P7/Q7 screening +2.82% FAIL; P8/Q6 screening +1.46% FAIL. Any P\u22648/Q\u22647 is dominated by failed P8/Q7, so P9/Q7 is minimal passing accumulator.\n", "tool_calls": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 2176, "prompt_tokens": 8247, "total_tokens": 10423, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1719}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 6769}}}
